        "content": "Insight\n\n12 February 2025\n\nUnited States Retail Market Dynamics Q4 2024\n\nRetail space crunch to ease as store closures free up 140 million square feet\n\nCapital flows\n\nLocation strategy\n\nRetail\n\nBusiness and professional services\n\nAuthors\n\nKeisha Virtue\n\nYour browser doesn't support speech synthesis.\n\nListen to article\u2022\n\nRead time:1 sec\n\nThe U.S. retail landscape is evolving rapidly, presenting both challenges and opportunities. Our latest report focuses on the ongoing supply crunch reshaping industry strategies.\n\nA persistent shortage of suitable space impacts expansion plans and market dynamics, with minimal near-term supply additions intensifying competition for prime locations. However, our forecast suggests a gradual loosening of construction activity in the coming years. Notably, an accelerated closure pipeline is set to inject over 140 million square feet back into the tight market, potentially alleviating some pressure.\n\nWhat does this mean for retailers, investors, and consumers? How will this supply dynamic influence retail strategies and consumer experiences? Our comprehensive analysis provides insights into these questions and more, offering a roadmap for navigating the complex retail terrain ahead.\n\nDiscover how industry leaders are adapting to these challenges in our full Q4 2024 United States Retail Market Dynamics. Don't miss the trends and forecasts shaping the retail sector's future.\n\nThe latest news, insights and opportunities from global commercial real estate markets straight to your inbox."
